From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weegee <748975+Weegee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:17:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] drv: no debug command on a powered-off chip, no
 watchdog after teardown

The debugfs file debug sent a firmware debug command without checking
that the firmware runs. Since the chip is powered off while idle and
its command memory and channels are freed on teardown, a write a few
seconds after the last stream dereferenced NULL.
fthd_isp_debug_cmd() now returns -EIO unless the firmware is up, like
fthd_isp_cmd().

fthd_hw_teardown() stopped the frame watchdog before it quiesced the
interrupt work, which re-arms the watchdog for every buffer it returns,
so the watchdog could stay queued after the teardown. It is now stopped
after the quiesce, and remove cancels it before dev_priv is freed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fthd_drv.c | 7 +++++--
 fthd_isp.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fthd_drv.c b/fthd_drv.c
index 41e0e70..5dd27a2 100644
--- a/fthd_drv.c
+++ b/fthd_drv.c
@@ -434,8 +434,9 @@ static void fthd_hw_teardown(struct fthd_private *dev_priv)
 		fthd_stop_firmware(dev_priv);
 
 	dev_priv->hw_state = FTHD_HW_DOWN;
-	fthd_frame_watchdog_stop(dev_priv);
 	fthd_hw_quiesce(dev_priv);
+	/* Only now: the irq work re-arms it for every buffer it returns */
+	fthd_frame_watchdog_stop(dev_priv);
 	/* Descriptors and IOMMU entries live in S2 memory */
 	fthd_v4l2_buffers_unmap(dev_priv);
 	isp_uninit(dev_priv);
@@ -718,9 +719,11 @@ static void fthd_pci_remove(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 
 	/*
 	 * A firmware stop that timed out in the teardown queued a recovery;
-	 * it must not run once dev_priv is freed.
+	 * it must not run once dev_priv is freed, and neither may a frame
+	 * watchdog that is still pending.
 	 */
 	cancel_work_sync(&dev_priv->recover_work);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dev_priv->frame_watchdog);
 
 	fthd_v4l2_unregister(dev_priv);
 
diff --git a/fthd_isp.c b/fthd_isp.c
index 2008431..0f781f0 100644
--- a/fthd_isp.c
+++ b/fthd_isp.c
@@ -370,6 +370,10 @@ int fthd_isp_debug_cmd(struct fthd_private *dev_priv, enum fthd_isp_cmds command
 	u32 entry;
 	int len, ret;
 
+	/* A powered off chip has no debug channel and no command memory */
+	if (dev_priv->hw_state != FTHD_HW_UP)
+		return -EIO;
+
 	memset(&cmd, 0, sizeof(cmd));
 
 	if (response_len) {
-- 
